# The project's runtime dependencies, which pyproject.toml declares with
# their floors, for the CI jobs that run or type-check the package. CI
# installs requirements-runtime.txt, this file compiled with hashes, with
# --require-hashes, then the project itself with --no-deps.
#
# Compile it on the NEWEST Python the tests matrix runs (3.15):
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes requirements-runtime.in
# pip-compile resolves for its own interpreter and drops a dependency whose
# marker is false there, and the lock must install on every matrix Python.
# A dependency only newer Pythons need (audioop-lts, which discord.py
# requires from 3.13 on) is kept only by a compile on a Python that needs
# it, and the marker on its line below keeps it off older ones. A backport
# only older Pythons need is listed here unconditionally instead, since a
# marker false on the compiling Python drops the line.
#
# This file sits here, not beside pyproject.toml, for the same reason:
# Dependabot compiles a directory holding pyproject.toml on the lowest Python
# its requires-python admits (3.11, which drops audioop-lts), and compiles
# this directory on the Python the lock's own header names.
discord.py
psutil
audioop-lts; python_version >= "3.13"
# aiohttp and aiosignal need it below Python 3.13.
typing-extensions
